{
  "_readme": [
    "Aion 2 wire layout for Aion2/Protocol/Aion2Protocol.cs. Everything the packet source knows about",
    "the game's frames lives here so a patch that shifts an opcode is a data fix, not a rebuild.",
    "calibrated=false means: nothing below has been verified against a real capture yet - the",
    "packet source then only reports that state and decodes nothing.",
    "",
    "Calibration procedure: run `Aion DPS.exe aion2-record fight.jsonl [port,...]` during a fight,",
    "then find the frame length prefix and the opcode families in the recording (damage numbers",
    "are the easiest anchor: look for the values the game showed on screen). Fill frame/opcodes/",
    "fields, set calibrated=true and gameVersion, and add the recording as a SelfCheck fixture.",
    "",
    "Field offsets are relative to the frame start (header included). Integer fields: offset+size",
    "(+signed). Strings: 2-byte char count followed by UTF-16LE at offset, or encoding=utf8z.",
    "flags.mask is a hex bitmask marking a critical hit.",
    "",
    "2026-09-30: calibrated against a real EU capture (game server port 13328, IP changes per server/session)",
    "and the in-game combat log. Framing is a LEB128 varint length: a record is length+prefixBytes-4 bytes",
    "long, the decoder sees it without the prefix, opcode = first 2 bytes big-endian. Frames with opcode 0xFFFF are bundles (u32 LE size + LZ4 block of further frames); only the damage",
    "frame (0x0438) is decoded so far, by the built-in layout named in damageLayout (see",
    "Aion2FrameDecoder.DecodeVarintDamage). 2026-10-02: damage-over-time ticks (0x0538) by dotLayout (Aion2FrameDecoder.DecodeVarintDot), entity hit points (0x008d) by hpLayout (Aion2FrameDecoder.DecodeHp). Not yet decoded: nickname/session (local player and names),",
    "DoT, heal-on-others, kill, hp, zone - candidates are noted in the project memory.",
    "syncOpcodes: all 330 opcodes seen in the captures so far (including those that occur once, such as the login lists, so a connection that starts with the login block can still be synchronised), nested bundle contents included. Used only to find a frame boundary when a capture starts mid-connection; normal operation accepts any opcode."
  ],
